sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 394-400: rhinoceros and allied skulls by coordinate-grid transformation (Osborn) — MorphoEval overall 65.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 (v1). Peak-picked grid intersections and arc-length skull boundaries on nine IA-pinned panels; greedy normalized-bbox matching (maxd=0.12). Primary Hyrachyus (394) -> Aceratherium (395): 40 matched nodes; TPS outline Procrustes 0.370 vs identity 0.377 vs affine 0.360 — TPS beats identity but affine wins on Procrustes. Six secondary pairs reported; 3/6 TPS beats identity. No parameter sweep completed (full 36 x all-pairs matrix hung). No shuffled-grid null, IoU, Pearson r, chamfer, or Jacobian check in the Pass 1 verdict file. Grid matching is automatic, not hand-labelled. Verdict in result.json: mixed. Overall 67.0/100. Overall 65.8/100 (faithfulness 59.9, reproducibility 79.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 530b3b50c; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.x (pip, requirements.txt lower bound >=1.7), scikit-image >=0.19, matplotlib >=3.3, Pillow >=8.0, lean 4.35.0 (elan stable). Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 42, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 87, Code-to-model traceability 81, Reproducibility package 73. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_055_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-055_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 530b3b50c, image/png, 540693 B, 1980×1100 px, artifact_sha256 65d3271d99b1aa5c2c476ae8f90ab25d1dfc51663e05b92ff0b626a382f24254 (sha256 65d3271d99b1aa5c2c476ae8f90ab25d1dfc51663e05b92ff0b626a382f24254), spec_fingerprint 1799c9e22b84705ed0af5fe44b5529c9ffab5f336a64446d6582253a48d2e8c1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1799c9e22b84705ed0af5fe44b5529c9ffab5f336a64446d6582253a48d2e8c1; artifact_sha256: 65d3271d99b1aa5c2c476ae8f90ab25d1dfc51663e05b92ff0b626a382f24254; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ceratotherium_simum_skull_mnhn_1400.jpg=7ed8c3776d2ab62a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p761_leaf0781_figs394-395.jpg=978a7d9039629c42..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p762_leaf0782_fig396.jpg=7a8a134814786620..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p763_leaf0783_figs397-398.jpg=229d3074b7e141bf..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p764_leaf0784_figs399-400.jpg=5dcb998220348ea5..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/t1917_055_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=ee9eba19f703221d...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Fig. 394 Hyrachyus skull with rectangular Cartesian grid; Fig. 395 Aceratherium in a deformed grid (p. 760-761) | occipital Aceratherium variants related by conformal transformations (Fig. 396, p. 762) | extensions to Titanotherium, tapir, horse, and rabbit by the same method (Figs. 397-400, pp. 763-764) | methodological claim that allied skulls differ by smooth coordinate transformation of a common diagram; reconstructed_in_script: phi as a thin-plate spline on automatically matched grid peaks (not digitised grid ink line-by-line) | skull outlines from largest connected component + arc-length semilandmarks | identity and affine-only controls; Procrustes distance as the sole quantitative fit statistic in Pass 1; transfer_boundary: Thompson's hand-placed grid correspondences are approximated by greedy NN on normalized bounding boxes | affine beating TPS on the primary pair weakens the claim that a non-affine TPS grid is necessary for Aceratherium; does_not_claim: that automatic grid matching equals Thompson's anatomical node pairing | that modern 3D geometric-morphometric datasets validate the rabbit/horse panels (Leporidae cache is a labelled mismatch) | that the Ceratotherium photograph (vendored) was analysed in Pass 1." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [digitisation/specimen-match, pressure P=2.5]: Hand-labelled or literature-backed grid correspondences vs automatic NN matching",
            "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Independent second assessor from a different provider",
            "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Numerical no-fold (Jacobian determinant) check of phi_t on the primary TPS grid",
            "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Shuffled-grid null; IoU, Pearson r, chamfer RMSE; report when affine beats TPS",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.5]: Primary-only sweep over maxd, TPS lambda, and boundary point count; report stability of TPS vs identity and vs affine",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=2.5]: Descriptive bone-vs-matrix CV on Ceratotherium simum MNHN photograph; enlarge control panel",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — this round is builder-scored'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Parameter-regime sweep (primary Hyrachyus->Aceratherium only): maxd in {0.08,0.10,0.12,0.15}, lambda in {0,1e-3,1e-2,0.01}, n_boundary in {80,120,160}; avoid all-pairs matrix that hung Pass 1'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Shuffled-grid null: permute target grid landmarks before TPS fit; compare Procrustes to nominal pairing'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Correspondence-free and coordinate goodness of fit: IoU of filled outlines, Pearson r, RMSE/centroid size, symmetric chamfer RMSE/centroid size'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Jacobian no-fold check of the primary TPS on a dense grid inside the skull (min det D phi_t over t in [0,1])'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Ceratotherium specimen bone-vs-matrix segmentation as descriptive CV (excluded from verdict); add shuffled control to comparison figure'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.658"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 1; second assessor pending)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://ai.google.dev> .
}

